  "summaries": {
    "en": "Shrine routing, weapon durability management, cooking efficiency, and Divine Beast preparation for a complete Breath of the Wild playthrough.",
    "ja": "祠ルーティング、武器耐久管理、料理効率化、神獣攻略準備まで、ブレス オブ ザ ワイルドを完走するための攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "adventure",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Weapon durability resets when enemies respawn at Blood Moon—stock up on high-damage weapons right before a Blood Moon triggers (watch for the crimson glow in the sky) to maintain a full weapon inventory.",
      "Cooking with Hyrule Bass + Hearty Radish creates Hearty Seafood Soup that adds 4 bonus heart containers; this is the most efficient survivability food early-game before unlocking high-level armour sets.",
      "Magnet rune conducts electricity—never use Magnet on metal objects during a thunderstorm if Link is wearing metal armour; this one-shots Link regardless of heart count.",
      "Climbing in rain is possible by using ice arrows on the wall surface to create footholds, or by waiting under a rock overhang for the rain to pass (rain cycles last 4–6 real-time minutes).",
      "Guardian Scouts in shrines and field Guardians have the same parry timing—master the blue-flash parry with a shield for a guaranteed one-shot deflect, eliminating the need for Ancient arrows."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "武器耐久はブラッドムーンで敵が復活するとリセットされる。空が赤く輝き始めたら、ブラッドムーン直前に高ダメージ武器を大量に入手して武器スロットを補充する。",
      "ハイラルバスとハートニンジンで「ハートたっぷりのシーフード煮」が作れる。ボーナスハート4個追加で序盤の最効率サバイバル食料。高レベル防具セットを揃えるまで常備する。",
      "マグネットルーンは電気を通す。雷雨中は金属防具を着たままでオブジェクトを持ち上げない。ハートの数に関係なく即死する。",
      "雨中の登攀は、アイスアローで壁に足場を作るか、岩の庇の下で雨が上がるまで待つ（リアル時間4〜6分）。",
      "祠のガーディアンもフィールドのガーディアンも同じパリィタイミングを持つ。青い閃光でシールドパリィを習得すれば、古代矢なしで確定ワンショット撃退できる。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Great Plateau Survival Priority",
        "body": "The Great Plateau introduces all four runes in a fixed order. After unlocking all four, prioritise cooking before leaving: the Forgotten Temple area has a camp fire and 8 cookable ingredients within 50 metres. Cook the coldproof elixir (3 Cold Darner bugs + any monster part) before attempting Mount Hylia—the cold damage there kills in 12 seconds without cold resistance. Collect 6 Boko Bows and 20 arrows before dropping off the Plateau; ranged combat is the safest approach against the first Lynel you encounter near Zora's Domain."
      },
      {
        "title": "First Shrine Routing Strategy",
        "body": "Target 20 shrines before approaching any Divine Beast—each 4-shrine Spirit Orb cluster provides one Heart Container or Stamina Vessel upgrade. The Akkala region (12 shrines) and Eldin region (10 shrines) have the highest density relative to area size. Use the Sheikah Sensor+ from Purah in Hateno Village (available after activating the Sheikah Tower) to auto-locate nearby shrines. The sensor range is 200 metres, covering most shrine density clusters in a single sweep."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Divine Beast Priority Order",
        "body": "Complete Divine Beasts in this order for the smoothest difficulty curve: Vah Medoh (easiest, Rito Village) → Vah Ruta (Zora's Domain, requires 20 ice arrows) → Vah Rudania (Goron City) → Vah Naboris (hardest, Gerudo). Each champion power-up received after defeating a Divine Beast Blights assists in the next fight. Daruk's Protection (Vah Rudania reward) blocks guardian attacks and makes the Vah Naboris approach across the electric sandstorm significantly safer."
      },
      {
        "title": "Stealth and Cooking Synergy",
        "body": "Sneaky Elixirs (Sunset Firefly × 3 + monster part) grant 3 levels of stealth for 8 minutes each. Stack stealth elixirs with the Sheikah Set to reach maximum stealth level, enabling full camp infiltration and horse theft from enemy camps. The most profitable stealth target in the mid-game is the Mounted Bokoblin camp east of Akkala Citadel: 8 high-tier weapons plus a Star Fragment spawn on the hill directly above at night."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Calamity Ganon Preparation",
        "body": "Calamity Ganon has 8 phantom forms in the first phase, each corresponding to a Divine Beast Blight boss. Each Blight you defeated beforehand reduces Calamity Ganon's total HP by 1/8th. Completing all four Divine Beasts cuts Ganon's starting HP by 50%. For Ganon's horse phase on Hyrule Field, the Ancient Bow with Ancient Arrows one-shots the horse form regardless of HP. Prepare 10+ Ancient Arrows, 20+ Hasty Elixirs for movement speed, and 15+ food items with 10+ hearts each."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Eating food to restore hearts when a monster is already attacking—food use animation takes 2 seconds and can be interrupted; always eat in a safe position before engaging.",
      "Using Stasis on enemies for extended periods without attacking—Stasis lasts only 10–15 seconds on large enemies; chain a full combo immediately after activation, not after repositioning.",
      "Attacking Taluses without aiming at the ore deposit weak point—body hits deal 1 damage regardless of weapon power; ore deposits deal 30–50× damage to Talus HP.",
      "Wasting Guardian Lasers by rolling—the deflect timing with a shield is 3 frames before laser contact; successfully deflecting one-shots the Guardian and preserves your weapon inventory.",
      "Entering Ganon without Champion abilities charged—all four champion abilities recharge on a timer; rest at an inn or shrine before the final battle to ensure full charges."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "敵に攻撃されている最中に食事を食べる。食べる動作は2秒かかり中断される。食事は安全な場所で戦闘前に摂る。",
      "ストップを敵に使って位置調整してから攻撃する。大型敵へのストップは10〜15秒しか続かない。発動直後にコンボを入れる。",
      "イワロックの体を攻撃する。体へのヒットは武器に関わらず1ダメージ。鉱石の弱点への攻撃は30〜50倍のダメージになる。",
      "ガーディアンのレーザーをころがりで回避する。シールドパリィのタイミングはレーザー着弾3フレーム前。成功すればガーディアンをワンショットで倒せる。",
      "勇者の力を溜めずにガノン戦に入る。4つの勇者の力はタイマーで再チャージされる。最終決戦前に宿屋か祠で休憩してフルチャージにする。"
    ]
  },
